CC   -!- FUNCTION: Part of the ABC transporter complex MalEFGK involved in
CC       maltose/maltodextrin import. Binds maltose and higher maltodextrins
CC       such as maltotriose. {ECO:0000269|PubMed:2026607,
CC       ECO:0000269|PubMed:2155217, ECO:0000269|PubMed:4215651,
CC       ECO:0000269|PubMed:776623}.
CC   -!- BIOPHYSICOCHEMICAL PROPERTIES:
CC       Kinetic parameters:
CC         KM=0.9 uM for maltose {ECO:0000269|PubMed:776623};
CC         KM=2 uM for maltotriose {ECO:0000269|PubMed:776623};
CC   -!- SUBUNIT: The complex is composed of two ATP-binding proteins (MalK),
CC       two transmembrane proteins (MalG and MalF) and a solute-binding protein
CC       (MalE). {ECO:0000269|PubMed:2026607, ECO:0000269|PubMed:2155217}.
CC   -!- INTERACTION:
CC       P0AEX9; P0A6F5: groEL; NbExp=3; IntAct=EBI-369910, EBI-543750;
CC       P0AEX9; P02916: malF; NbExp=5; IntAct=EBI-369910, EBI-1118919;
CC   -!- SUBCELLULAR LOCATION: Periplasm {ECO:0000269|PubMed:4215651}.
CC   -!- INDUCTION: Induced by maltose and the transcriptional regulator MalT
CC       (PubMed:4215651). Permanently repressed by cold shock in a PNPase-
CC       dependent fashion (PubMed:14527658). {ECO:0000269|PubMed:14527658,
CC       ECO:0000269|PubMed:4215651}.
CC   -!- SIMILARITY: Belongs to the bacterial solute-binding protein 1 family.
CC       {ECO:0000305}.
